From 3eeb6a9f1a12acf67761e60c8002275b0e6c3002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Forst <ensonador@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:52:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] ui.c: letting go of a held step closes its SEL list

The held step's SEL list is not a mode of its own: list_build rebuilds
it from ui.held on every draw. Releasing the step cleared ui.held,
lockpg and trickpg but left lst.open set, so the next repaint turned the
step's menu into the Steps page's pattern list (PATTERN, LENGTH, SCALE,
...) instead of going back to the page.

The last held step's release now closes the list (with more steps still
held it stays, on the one left, as before).

tests/scenarios/heldsteplist.xy: once the step is let go, SELECT turns
the Steps page to Bar instead of scrolling the stale list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 app/ui.c                        |  5 +++--
 tests/scenarios/heldsteplist.xy | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/ui.c b/app/ui.c
index db994a6..ae501ab 100644
--- a/app/ui.c
+++ b/app/ui.c
@@ -1625,9 +1625,10 @@ static void key_up(int k)
         if (!ui.held_used && !ui.held_multi && plat_ms() - ui.key_t[k] < STEP_TAP_MS)
             step_toggle(w);                      /* a tap; a longer hold only looked at the step */
         ui.held &= (uint16_t)~(1u << w);
-        if (!ui.held)                            /* (chord mode stays on past the step's own release) */
+        if (!ui.held) {                          /* (chord mode stays on past the step's own release) */
             ui.lockpg = ui.trickpg = 0;
-        else
+            lst.open = 0;                        /* its SEL list is the held step's: let go, and it goes */
+        } else
             for (int i = 0; i < 16; i++)
                 if (ui.held >> i & 1u) {
                     ui.held_first = (uint8_t)i;
diff --git a/tests/scenarios/heldsteplist.xy b/tests/scenarios/heldsteplist.xy
index d21a896..0c806af 100644
--- a/tests/scenarios/heldsteplist.xy
+++ b/tests/scenarios/heldsteplist.xy
@@ -18,3 +18,14 @@ wait 60
 expect note 2 1 1 60
 release EDIT
 key w0 up
+# letting the step go closes its list: back on Steps (SELECT turns its page, not the list's rows)
+wait 60
+key w1 down
+wait 60
+tap SEL
+wait 60
+key w1 up
+wait 60
+spin SELECT 1
+wait 60
+expect page Bar
